# Generated from: specs/236-adopt-github-blocked-by-as-the-only-issue-dependency-type/requirements.md
Feature: GitHub blocked-by as the sole issue dependency
  As a developer running nmg-sdlc in Oh My Pi or Herdr
  I want issue sequencing to use only GitHub official blocked-by
  So that every lifecycle surface shares one fail-closed graph

  # --- Happy Path ---

  @SCN001
  Scenario: official blocked-by is the sole dependency authority
    Given an nmg-sdlc issue graph
    When a lifecycle surface reads or writes dependencies
    Then it uses only GitHub official blocked-by
    And body relations, spike relations, sub-issues, and labels do not affect eligibility

  @SCN002
  Scenario: draft applies approved blocked-by edges
    Given an approved split topology or explicit sequencing against named existing issues
    When draft-issue creates the issues
    Then it preflights the combined graph and applies official blocked-by edges
    And it requires no confirmation beyond split and final plan approval
    And it does not generate body relation lines

  @SCN003
  Scenario: upgrade screens and reconciles every issue
    Given official dependencies, legacy fields, or clear sequencing language
    When the dependency-graph upgrade category is detected and approved
    Then every repository issue and official edge is screened
    And missing official edges with explicit evidence are added
    And dangling targets and open cycles are refused before writing

  @SCN004
  Scenario: execute presents only eligible issues
    Given open spec-created issues with mixed dependency status
    When /sdlc-execute runs without arguments
    Then only readable unblocked acyclic issues are presented
    And zero eligible issues print the existing empty message without a picker

  # --- Alternative Paths ---

  @SCN005
  Scenario Outline: graph status controls execution
    Given issue 42 has <graphState>
    When explicit execute or start validates issue 42
    Then the result is <result>
    And mutation is <mutation>

    Examples:
      | graphState | result | mutation |
      | no blocked-by edges | eligible | allowed after validation |
      | only closed blockers | eligible | allowed after validation |
      | an open blocker | dependency_blocked | forbidden |
      | a dangling target | dependency_dangling | forbidden |
      | an open cycle | dependency_cycle | forbidden |
      | unreadable evidence | dependency_unreadable | forbidden |

  # --- Error Handling ---

  @SCN006
  Scenario: unreadable dependency evidence fails closed
    Given a dependency response is incomplete, malformed, or unreadable
    When any lifecycle surface needs the graph
    Then it reports dependency_unreadable
    And it does not infer eligibility from body text or partial pages

  # --- Edge Cases ---

  @SCN007
  Scenario: cycles are deterministic and closed blockers are satisfied
    Given a graph containing closed blocker edges and a cycle among open issues
    When the shared validator runs
    Then closed blocker edges do not block independent execution
    And the open cycle is rejected with a canonical cycle path
